$meta
  title = Tech Finder — find your laptop's charger, specs & compatible parts
  description = Type a laptop model (or snap a photo of its spec label / charger tip) to get a cited spec sheet, the exact charger/connector it needs, and compatible RAM / SSD / battery options with buy links.
  tags = tech finder, laptop, charger, adapter, specs, power supply
  header
    mode = minimal

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// FEATURE DEPLOYMENT PLAN — AI Tech Finder (atomic roadmap v1.0)
// Source: scratch/message-attachments/ai-tech-finder-app-atomic-roadmap.markdown
// (that file is ephemeral — this comment block is the durable home of the plan)
//
// WORKFLOW RULES
// 1. STRICT HOLD — do NOT implement any task until the user explicitly says the
//    backlog is complete.
// 2. Then pick ONLY the first uncompleted task (PART or TODO) below, in order.
// 3. Implement that single task, write validation tests for it, flip it to DONE,
//    and STOP for review before starting the next task.
//
// LEGEND:  DONE = fully implemented in the prototype · PART = partial / lighter
//          TODO = not built yet
//
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// PHASE 1 — DEVICE IDENTIFICATION & INPUT
// - DONE 1. Implement Text-Based Search ........... src/app.js searchInput → identifyProduct
// - DONE 2. Normalize Model Numbers ............... src/app.js identifyProduct (token/number normalization)
// - DONE 3. Implement Image Upload Pipeline ....... photo upload → runVision (browser-local, not stored)
// - DONE 4. Integrate OCR/Visual Recognition ...... runVision via generateText multimodal (label + barrel tip)
// - DONE 5. Resolve Device Ambiguity .............. disambiguation pick-list cards when multiple candidates
// - DONE 6. Validate Device Identity .............. state.product (catalog id) is the key for all lookups
//
// PHASE 2 — TECHNICAL SPECIFICATION ENGINE
// - DONE 7. Retrieve Core Hardware Specs .......... data.js — Processor (chip/cores/threads/clock) + RAM + storage rows on all 10; Apple verified, others amber
// - DONE 8. Retrieve Display & Physical Specs ..... data.js — panel/resolution + weight + dimensions on all 10; Apple verified, others amber
// - DONE 9. Map Power Requirements ............... data.js power (conn, watts) + CONN_KB
// - DONE 10. Map I/O and Connectivity ............ data.js — ports w/ versions + OS support row on all 10; Apple verified, others amber
// - DONE 11. Implement Source Traceability ........ per-row vf/source flags + per-source URLs, amber "unverified" defaults
// - DONE 12. Format Specification Output ......... Markdown + CSV report builders (src/app.js)
//
// PHASE 3 — COMPATIBILITY & PARTS MATCHING
// - DONE 13. Define Compatibility Constraints .... fitRules / rankedAdapters — deterministic, LLM never decides fit
// - DONE 14. Match OEM Parts .................... DB.ADAPTERS: OEM adapter for every catalog device (HP 65W USB-C added) + live-extract sheet for out-of-catalog
// - DONE 15. Match Aftermarket Equivalents ...... 3rd-party adapters verified on Amazon.ca for usbc / dell74 / hpSmart / lenovoSlim (each cited)
// - DONE 16. Match Upgrade Components ........... "Parts & upgrades" tab (RAM / M.2 SSD)
// - DONE 17. Resolve Vendor Links ............... Canada-first: Amazon.ca / Memory Express / Shopbot.ca (links only)
// - DONE 18. Generate Parts Compatibility Report . per-part cards with reason-for-fit + vendor links + MD export
//
// PHASE 4 — VENDOR & PRICING INTEGRATION
// - DONE 19. Vendor Search Integration .......... "Find live listings" per part card — live Amazon.ca search via superFetch (parsed product pages), Bing vendor-site fallback; no prices shown
// - DONE 20. Price & Availability Aggregation .... availability half built: per-listing live health check + availability summary (price half deliberately out of scope — no-price-claims rule)
// - DONE 21. Link Validation Logic .............. verifyAllLinks: HTTP re-checks every source AND every vendor/part buy link; session-cached status dots on all links (Sources tab + buy buttons)
// - DONE 22. Vendor Result Mapping by price ...... availability-ranked mapping (responding listings first) + per-listing status dots; "by price" clause out of scope (no price claims)
// - DONE 23. Currency Normalization (→ CAD) ...... cadUrl: every shopping link normalized to a Canadian store (Dell OEM /en-us/shop|/laptop → /en-ca) + "· CAD" label on every buy button (price-conversion half out of scope — no-price-claims rule)
// - DONE 24. Dead-Link Handling ................. dead (404/410/451) vs warn (bot-block) vs unreach statuses on all link checks; dead links strikethrough-flagged (sources + buy buttons); dead-link summary banner; Amazon live listings quote out-of-stock from the vendor page
//
// PHASE 5 — RESULTS PRESENTATION
// - DONE 25. Specification Sheet Rendering ...... spec-sheet tab, read-only, copyable plain text
// - DONE 26. Compatible Part Card Display ....... adapter/part cards: part number, reason, links
// - PART 27. Spec Sheet Export ................. Markdown + CSV; PDF not yet
// - DONE 28. Clipboard Integration .............. "Copy report (MD)" + per-part copy
// - TODO 29. Part Comparison View ............... not built
// - PART 30. Result State Management ........... no-match → live web fallback; vendor-failed states partial
//
// PHASE 6 — KNOWLEDGE BASE & DATA MANAGEMENT
// - DONE 31. Schema Definition ................. TFDB in src/data.js (products / adapters / CONN_KB / SRC)
// - TODO 32. Record Management ................. not built — catalog is hand-edited; no versioning UI
// - PART 33. Alias & Deduplication Logic ....... identifyProduct token matching; no alias table
// - PART 34. Source Credibility Scoring ........ vf:true (fetch-confirmed) vs unverified amber dots
// - TODO 35. Stale Data Handling ............... not built
// - DONE 36. Cross-Reference Validation ........ fit rules re-check connector + voltage + wattage per part
//
// PHASE 7 — CONVERSATIONAL ASSISTANT & QUERY HANDLING
// - TODO 37. Natural Language Intent Parsing .... not built (single-shot search form)
// - TODO 38. Conversation Context Tracking ...... not built
// - PART 39. Ambiguity Resolution .............. pick-list cards (search); no NL clarifying turns
// - TODO 40. Part Compatibility Synthesis (NL) .. not built (deterministic rules path exists)
// - TODO 41. Answer Synthesis (NL) ............. not built
// - PART 42. Query Fallback Logic .............. live web-retrieval fallback for out-of-catalog; NL path no
//
// PHASE 8 — QUALITY, TRUST & SAFETY
// - DONE 43. Hardware Constraint Verification ... fit engine — ANY violated constraint excludes the part
// - TODO 44. Confidence Scoring System ......... not built (binary confirmed/unverified only)
// - DONE 45. User Validation Loop .............. live-extract sheet: per-row "confirm" flips green + flags data
// - TODO 46. Catalog Synchronization .......... not built
// - PART 47. Safety Guardrail Enforcement ...... part-number "never order from memory" warnings; formal intercept pending
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

generateText = {import:ai-text-plugin}
superFetch = {import:super-fetch-plugin}
